  "Description": {
    "Cost": 8479072,
    "UIName": "Gatekeeper",
    "Id": "chassisdef_gatekeeper_GKP-Prime",
    "Name": "Gatekeeper",
    "Details": "Developed by the Society following the successful deployment of the Pulsar, the Gatekeeper is an Assault OmniMech based on the Clan Warhawk. The Prime configuration is built for long-range fire support, mounting four ER PPCs backed by an extensive array of heat sinks capable of sustaining repeated volleys. A pod-mounted Nova CEWS replaces the targeting computer normally associated with the Warhawk, providing advanced electronic warfare capabilities. Gatekeepers rarely see offensive combat, instead serving as heavily armed sentinels concealed around important Society facilities.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Protected Actuators</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 1.19</color></b>\n\n<color=#FFEF00>Arm Actuator Limits: Omni</color>",
    "Icon": "Gatekeeper"
  },
  "VariantName": "GKP-Prime",
  "ChassisTags": {
    "items": [
      "ArmLimitUpperLeft",
      "ArmLimitUpperRight",
      "OmniMech",
      "SocietyMech",
      "mr-resize-1.10-1.04-1.10"
    ]
  },
  "StockRole": "Sniper",
  "YangsThoughts": "Those Society scientists really took the Warhawk's firepower to another level. Four ER PPCs is impressive enough, but they packed in enough heat sinks to keep firing them without cooking the mech! Just don't expect to do it on the move—the Gatekeeper needs to stay planted to make full use of that cooling.",
